  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Management and Training obligated $281M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Management and Training received 35 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $8M and obligations up 33.6% year over year. Management and Training saw the largest single buyer as the Department of Labor, which obligated $248M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $33.1M. Management and Training’s primary market is Other Technical and Trade Schools with $248M in obligations, followed by Security Guards and Patrol Services with $33.1M. Management and Training’s obligations by fiscal year show year totals of $382M in FY21, $267M in FY22, $259M in FY23, $234M in FY24, $211M in FY25, and $281M in FY26 to date. Management and Training’s current-year totals are partial, covering the fiscal year to date, and award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than obligation flows. This snapshot summarizes who the buyer is, which markets receive funds, and how current obligations compare to prior fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations changed over the past six fiscal years?",
        "body": "Management and Training obligated $382M in FY21, $267M in FY22, $259M in FY23, $234M in FY24, $211M in FY25, and $281M in FY26 to date. Management and Training’s FY26 obligations are up 33.6% year over year. Management and Training’s current-year total is partial and covers the fiscal year to date. Management and Training’s FY21 total remains the largest single-year obligation in this six-year series."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and what markets receive the most obligations?",
        "body": "Management and Training’s top buying agency is the Department of Labor with $248M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $33.1M. Management and Training’s top market is Other Technical and Trade Schools with $248M, followed by Security Guards and Patrol Services with $33.1M. Management and Training’s market and agency rankings reflect the same two dollar figures at the top of each list."
      }
    ]
